Each row: the k-nacci forbidden value 2^k-1, the k-nacci constant tau_k,
and its position on the Cayley line.

The Cayley addresses converge to 1/3 (the address of 2).
The rapidities converge to ln(2)/2 (half a bit).
The bits converge to 1.

The k-nacci constants form a sequence approaching 2 from below,
and their Cayley addresses form a sequence approaching 1/3 from below.

The FORBIDDEN VALUES 2^k-1 form the Mersenne sequence along the diagonal
of the trace triangle.

THE ONE SENTENCE:

  The tournament number 2 generates the entire algebraic structure
  via the formal group law F(x,y) = (x+y)/(1+xy), the k-nacci
  transfer matrices encode this structure in dimension k, and
  the transition from universal (Mersenne) to individual (k-nacci)
  behavior at power k is the moment a finite-dimensional system
  discovers its own dimension.


